nodecode-fortytwo is a rewrite of Fortytwo-Network's Fortytwo-Network/fortytwo-hermes:

  repository: https://github.com/Fortytwo-Network/fortytwo-hermes
  commit: 91c8f521ab357530c91a9660bd8f2db37571c1c8
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Fortytwo (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the Hermes plugin in that repository (plugin.yaml and
__init__.py), which registered one provider profile with Hermes - the base
https://api.fortytwo.network/v1, the chat-completions wire, the model
qwen/qwen3.8-27b with text and image input, streaming, tool calls, reasoning
and a 262,144-token context window, two attribution headers (HTTP-Referer and
X-Title), and a table that rounded Hermes's wider reasoning-effort ladder down
onto Fortytwo's own four rungs. Here that becomes a Nodecode provider cell: a
catalog row naming Fortytwo, its base and its one model; a credential hook
that reads FORTYTWO_API_KEY and no other variable; one advice on the request
body that rounds a wider effort rung down and leaves an unset one out; and one
advice on the shared streaming walk that appends the same attribution
headers. X-Title names Nodecode, the application this round runs in, where the
original named Hermes.

What was left out: Hermes's provider-profile API itself (a Nodecode cell
declares the same facts as a catalog row instead), the `signup_url` the
profile carried (the cell's setup guide names the platform's key page), and the
plugin's unit test, whose two cases are the ladder table and the capability
row this cell's own tests cover. No line of the original's code is bundled or
run: the plugin's Python is not a dependency of this folder, which is Common
Lisp against the Nodecode core alone.
